<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  The address book lives on the phone (IndexedDB in the app's WebView), and
  BlackBook has no account at all: `noAccounts` in src/main.tsx (2026-10-20)
  removes sign-in, and with it the SDK's signed-in "app opened" event and its
  anonymous daily open count. Nothing about the book is sent to us.

  The encrypted online copy (public.blackbook_vaults) went with sign-in on
  2026-10-20. In its place the user can save a backup file (optionally
  encrypted with a password, AES-256-GCM under PBKDF2-SHA-256), which goes
  only where the user sends it through the share sheet.

  The phone's contacts ("From my contacts", "Import my phone contacts") are
  read on the phone, only when the user asks, and never written to. What is
  read becomes part of the local book and leaves the phone only inside a
  backup or CSV file the user saves, so Contacts is not declared as collected.

  So no data is collected and none is declared. Nothing is used for tracking,
  and there are no third-party analytics or advertising SDKs.

  Required-reason APIs: @capacitor/filesystem (used to hand a CSV export or a
  backup file to the share sheet) can read file creation and modification dates (its `stat`),
  only on files in the app's own container, and neither it nor its
  IONFilesystemLib pod ships a manifest. Capacitor's core frameworks carry
  their own manifests, and @capacitor/share, @capacitor-community/contacts and
  the SDK's UnisimSdk pod use none of the listed APIs.

  Keep this in step with PRIVACY.md, store-assets/data-safety.json and the
  App Store Connect privacy answers.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- @capacitor/filesystem's stat: files in the app container. C617.1. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
